 M. &#x00026; Rizzo, A. A., virtual reality in brain damage rehabilitation: review</article-title><source><italic>CyberPsychology &#x00026; Behavior</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>8</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>271</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pfurtscheller</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Neuper</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Motor imagery and direct brain-computer communication</article-title><source><italic>Proceedings of the IEEE</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>89</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>1123</fpage><lpage>1134</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolpaw</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Birbaumer</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>McFarland</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfurtscheller</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughan</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Brain-computer interfaces for communication and control</article-title><source><italic>Clinical Neurophysiology</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>113</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>767</fpage><lpage>791</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12048038</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lalor</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelly</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Finucane</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Steady-state VEP-based brain-computer interface control in an immersive 3D gaming environment</article-title><source>